# Upload filter for `railway up --no-gitignore`.
#
# Why --no-gitignore is needed: the Railway CLI honours .gitignore when it
# builds the upload tarball, and demo-corpus/ is deliberately gitignored (119 MB
# of generated image blobs, far past the 30 KB commit limit). Uploading with the
# default behaviour silently shipped a build context WITHOUT the corpus, the
# Dockerfile's COPY landed an empty directory, and the deployed site served
# `manifest_sources=0` — a green deploy that quietly did nothing.
#
# So we disable the .gitignore filter and re-exclude the heavy paths here. Keep
# this in sync with .dockerignore for anything that must never reach the build.
target/
.git/
.jj/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
.workongoing
.env
.env.local
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
**/.DS_Store
